IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cpp-core-application`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 98 to 101 -- THE SOCIAL INSURANCE NUMBER.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2677 to 2708 of the Act file.
--
-- Section 98 makes three kinds of individual apply for a Social Insurance Number (one who applies to divide
-- pensionable earnings, one who reaches eighteen and works in pensionable employment, one who must file a
-- return of self-employed earnings), makes the Minister assign it, and makes the employer ask the employee for
-- the number and the employee give it. Section 99 says how the application is signed and when a changed name
-- must be reported. Section 100 lets the Minister agree with a province to assign numbers for it and deems such a
-- number assigned under this Act. Section 101 is a regulation-making power (inert, see NOTES.md).
--
-- DUTIES ARE WRITTEN AS A YES/NO "the duty arises" RULE AND A DATE "the last day" RULE, as the core does for
-- section 3(2): the stable binary has no useful way to assert a regulative value, and the date rules are what a
-- person asks ("by when?"). Thirty days after a day is that day plus 30 (the core's calendar, fork C6-F9).
--
-- THE JURAL RELATIONS (NOTES.md has the table):
--   s 98(1) to (3)  the individual's duty to apply (the Minister's claim); the individual's power to apply and
--                   the Minister's duty to assign (s 98(4)); the Minister's liberty to issue a Card.
--   s 98(5)         the employer's duty to require the number (the employee's liability to be required) and to record it.
--   s 98(6)         the employee's duty to inform the employer (the employer's claim).
--   s 99(1)         a condition on the individual's application: the Minister's no-duty to act on one not signed as stated.
--   s 99(2)         the individual's duty to tell the Minister a new name (the Minister's claim).
--   s 100(1)        the Minister's power to agree with a province (the province's liability to be agreed with).
--   s 100(2)        a deeming rule: a number assigned under an agreement counts as assigned under this Act.
--
-- Out of range, taken as inputs: section 30 (the duty to file a return) and section 33 (the day payment is due), piece cp2;
-- "pensionable employment", section 6(1), piece cp1; the prescribed form and manner (the Regulations carry none: regulation 88,
-- piece cr1, says only that the Minister may cause a number to be assigned and a Card issued).
-- Section 4(1)(a) of the Act takes "the provisions of Part III with respect to employees in pensionable employment" out of employment in a province
-- providing a comprehensive pension plan, unless section 4(2) treats the employment as employment elsewhere. Those provisions are subsections 98(2), (5) and
-- (6) and 99(2)(a) and (b) (fork C6-F14): subsection 98(2) and the record-keeping duty of 98(5) call the core's section 4(1)(a) rule; subsection 98(5)'s
-- duty to require the number takes subsection 98(2)'s result; subsection 98(6) follows from the requirement; and in subsection 99(2) "employed in pensionable
-- employment" means employment to which Part III reaches, which the caller decides with the same core rule.
-- Ages go through the core's section 2(2): section 98 is not one of the ten provisions it excepts, so a person is
-- treated as reaching eighteen on the first day of the month after the month of the eighteenth birthday (fork C6-F6).

§ `Part III -- the Social Insurance Number (sections 98 to 101)`

§§ `Not a provision: has a number already been assigned?`

-- Sections 98(1), (2) and (3) each apply only "if he has not earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number".
-- A number counts if it was assigned under the authority of an Act of Parliament (section 2(1) "Social Insurance
-- Number") or caused to be assigned by the Minister under an agreement (section 100(2)).
GIVEN `a number was assigned to the individual under the authority of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to the individual under an agreement entered into under subsection 100(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` `a number was assigned to the individual under the authority of an Act of Parliament` `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to the individual under an agreement entered into under subsection 100(1)` MEANS
        `s 2(1) — a Social Insurance Number` `a number was assigned to the individual under the authority of an Act of Parliament`
    OR  `s 100(2) — a number caused to be assigned under an agreement is deemed to have been assigned under this Act` `the Minister caused a number to be assigned to the individual under an agreement entered into under subsection 100(1)`

§§ `Section 98 -- the application for a Social Insurance Number`

-- Subsections 98(1), (2) and (3) each say the application is filed "in such form and manner as may be prescribed".
-- Section 2(1) "prescribed": a form is prescribed when the Minister authorizes it; a manner when a regulation prescribes it.
-- The Regulations among the inputs prescribe neither (fork C6-F10), so both are yes/no inputs.
-- src:2677 | Application for assignment of Social Insurance Number
-- src:2678 | 98 (1) Every individual who applies for a division under section 55 or 55.1 shall, within thirty days of the date of application for such division, if he has not earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number, file an application with the Minister, in such form and manner as may be prescribed, for the assignment to him of a Social Insurance Number.
@ref Act s 98(1) (src:2677-2678)
GIVEN `the form is one the Minister authorizes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner is one a regulation prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(1) to (3) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is in the prescribed form and manner` `the form is one the Minister authorizes` `the manner is one a regulation prescribes` MEANS
        `s 2(1) — prescribed` `a form or the information to be given on a form` `the form is one the Minister authorizes` FALSE FALSE
    AND `s 2(1) — prescribed` `any other matter` FALSE `the manner is one a regulation prescribes` FALSE

-- The individual to whom subsection (1) applies: one who applies for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings
-- under section 55 or 55.1 (out of range: sections 55 and 55.1 (piece cp3)).
@ref Act s 98(1) (src:2678)
GIVEN `the individual applies for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(1) — subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` `the individual applies for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` MEANS
    `the individual applies for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1`

@ref Act s 98(1) (src:2678)
GIVEN `subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(1) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number` `subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` MEANS
    `subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` AND NOT `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number`

-- "within thirty days of the date of application for such division".
@ref Act s 98(1) (src:2678)
GIVEN `the date of the application for the division` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 98(1) — the last day for filing the application` `the date of the application for the division` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the date of the application for the division` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 30)

-- Only the end of the thirty days is stated; the text sets no earliest day (fork C6-F9).
@ref Act s 98(1) (src:2678)
GIVEN `the date of the application for the division` IS A DATE
      `the day the application for a number is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(1) — an application filed on a day is filed in time` `the date of the application for the division` `the day the application for a number is filed` MEANS
    `the day the application for a number is filed` AT MOST (`s 98(1) — the last day for filing the application` `the date of the application for the division`)

-- src:2679 | Idem
-- src:2680 | (2) Every individual who reaches eighteen years of age and is or becomes employed in pensionable employment on or after reaching that age shall, within thirty days after he reaches eighteen years of age or becomes employed in pensionable employment, as the case may be, if he has not earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number, file an application with the Minister, in such form and manner as may be prescribed, for the assignment to him of a Social Insurance Number.
@ref Act s 98(2) (src:2679-2680)
GIVEN `employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holding an office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is or becomes so employed on or after reaching eighteen years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 4(2) treats the employment as employment in another province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(2) — subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` `employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `holding an office` `the employment is pensionable employment` `the individual is or becomes so employed on or after reaching eighteen years of age` `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `subsection 4(2) treats the employment as employment in another province` MEANS
    -- "employed in pensionable employment": employment under section 2(1) that is pensionable employment (out of range: section 6(1) (piece cp1)).
        `s 2(1) — employment` `employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `holding an office`
    AND `the employment is pensionable employment`
    AND `the individual is or becomes so employed on or after reaching eighteen years of age`
    -- Section 4(1)(a): "the provisions of Part III with respect to employees in pensionable employment do not apply in relation
    -- to employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan", except as section 4(2) provides (fork C6-F14).
    -- Subsections 98(5) and (6) and 99(2) are the other such provisions; they are gated by this rule or take its result as an input.
    AND `s 4(1)(a) — the Act's provisions on employee and employer contributions reach the employment` `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `subsection 4(2) treats the employment as employment in another province`

-- "after he reaches eighteen years of age": section 2(2) applies (fork C6-F6), so it is the first day of the month after
-- the month of the eighteenth birthday.
@ref Act s 98(2) (src:2679-2680)
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 98(2) — the day the individual is treated as reaching eighteen years of age` `date of birth` MEANS
    `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` 18

-- "within thirty days after he reaches eighteen years of age or becomes employed in pensionable employment, as the case
-- may be": the thirty days run from whichever of the two happens later (fork C6-F5; section 98(5) says "whichever is the later").
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day the individual became employed in pensionable employment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of the day an individual reaches eighteen and the day the individual becomes employed in pensionable employment` `date of birth` `the day the individual became employed in pensionable employment` MEANS
    IF `s 98(2) — the day the individual is treated as reaching eighteen years of age` `date of birth` AT LEAST `the day the individual became employed in pensionable employment`
    THEN `s 98(2) — the day the individual is treated as reaching eighteen years of age` `date of birth`
    ELSE `the day the individual became employed in pensionable employment`

@ref Act s 98(2) (src:2679-2680)
GIVEN `subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(2) — the individual must file an application for a Social Insurance Number` `subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` MEANS
    `subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` AND NOT `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number`

@ref Act s 98(2) (src:2679-2680)
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day the individual became employed in pensionable employment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 98(2) — the last day for filing the application` `date of birth` `the day the individual became employed in pensionable employment` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends`
        (`the later of the day an individual reaches eighteen and the day the individual becomes employed in pensionable employment` `date of birth` `the day the individual became employed in pensionable employment`)
        (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 30)

-- src:2681 | Application — individual with self-employed earnings
-- src:2682 | (3) Every individual who is required by section 30 to file a return of their self-employed earnings for a year, other than an individual to whom subsection (1) or (2) applies, shall on or before the first day on or before which they are required by section 33 to pay any amount as or on account of the contributions required to be made by them for that year in respect of those earnings, if they have not earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number, apply to the Minister, in the form and manner that may be prescribed, for the assignment to them of a Social Insurance Number.
@ref Act s 98(3) (src:2681-2682)
GIVEN `section 30 requires the individual to file a return of self-employed earnings for a year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(3) — the individual must apply for a Social Insurance Number` `section 30 requires the individual to file a return of self-employed earnings for a year` `subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` `subsection 98(2) applies to the individual` `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` MEANS
    -- out of range: section 30 (piece cp2)
        `section 30 requires the individual to file a return of self-employed earnings for a year`
    -- "other than an individual to whom subsection (1) or (2) applies"
    AND NOT (`subsection 98(1) applies to the individual` OR `subsection 98(2) applies to the individual`)
    AND NOT `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number`

-- "on or before the first day on or before which they are required by section 33 to pay any amount ...".
-- out of range: section 33 (piece cp2)
@ref Act s 98(3) (src:2681-2682)
GIVEN `the first day on or before which section 33 requires the individual to pay any amount on account of the contributions for the year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 98(3) — the last day for applying` `the first day on or before which section 33 requires the individual to pay any amount on account of the contributions for the year` MEANS
    `the first day on or before which section 33 requires the individual to pay any amount on account of the contributions for the year`

-- src:2683 | Assignment of Number
-- src:2684 | (4) The Minister shall, on application by an individual to whom a Social Insurance Number has not earlier been assigned, cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to the individual and a Social Insurance Number Card may be issued to the individual.
@ref Act s 98(4) (src:2683-2684)
GIVEN `the individual has applied for a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(4) — the Minister must cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to the individual` `the individual has applied for a Social Insurance Number` `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` MEANS
    `the individual has applied for a Social Insurance Number` AND NOT `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number`

-- "a Social Insurance Number Card may be issued to the individual": a permission of the Minister, on the same facts.
@ref Act s 98(4) (src:2683-2684)
GIVEN `the individual has applied for a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(4) — a Social Insurance Number Card may be issued to the individual` `the individual has applied for a Social Insurance Number` `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number` MEANS
    `s 98(4) — the Minister must cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to the individual` `the individual has applied for a Social Insurance Number` `the individual has earlier been assigned a Social Insurance Number`

-- src:2685 | Employer to maintain record of Social Insurance Number
-- src:2686 | (5) Every employer who employs an employee in pensionable employment shall, in the case of an employee to whom subsection (2) applies, within 30 days after the day on which the employee reaches 18 years of age or becomes employed in pensionable employment, whichever is the later, require the employee to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number, and the employer shall maintain a record of the Social Insurance Number of each employee.
@ref Act s 98(5) (src:2685-2686)
GIVEN `the employer employs the employee in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 98(2) applies to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(5) — the employer must require the employee to inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` `the employer employs the employee in pensionable employment` `subsection 98(2) applies to the employee` MEANS
    `the employer employs the employee in pensionable employment` AND `subsection 98(2) applies to the employee`

-- "within 30 days after the day on which the employee reaches 18 years of age or becomes employed in pensionable
-- employment, whichever is the later".
@ref Act s 98(5) (src:2685-2686)
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day the employee became employed in pensionable employment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 98(5) — the last day on which the employer must require the employee to inform the employer` `date of birth` `the day the employee became employed in pensionable employment` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends`
        (`the later of the day an individual reaches eighteen and the day the individual becomes employed in pensionable employment` `date of birth` `the day the employee became employed in pensionable employment`)
        (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 30)

-- "the employer shall maintain a record of the Social Insurance Number of each employee": read as each employee the
-- employer employs in pensionable employment (fork C6-F7).
@ref Act s 98(5) (src:2685-2686)
GIVEN `the employer employs the employee in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 4(2) treats the employment as employment in another province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(5) — the employer must maintain a record of the employee's Social Insurance Number` `the employer employs the employee in pensionable employment` `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `subsection 4(2) treats the employment as employment in another province` MEANS
        `the employer employs the employee in pensionable employment`
    -- section 4(1)(a) takes Part III's provisions about employees in pensionable employment out of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan (fork C6-F14)
    AND `s 4(1)(a) — the Act's provisions on employee and employer contributions reach the employment` `the employment is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `subsection 4(2) treats the employment as employment in another province`

-- src:2687 | Employee to provide Social Insurance Number
-- src:2688 | (6) Every employee who is required under subsection (5) to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number shall do so within 30 days after the day on which they are required to do so by the employer.
@ref Act s 98(6) (src:2687-2688)
GIVEN `the employer requires the employee under subsection 98(5) to inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 98(6) — the employee must inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` `the employer requires the employee under subsection 98(5) to inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number` MEANS
    `the employer requires the employee under subsection 98(5) to inform the employer of the employee's Social Insurance Number`

@ref Act s 98(6) (src:2687-2688)
GIVEN `the day the employer requires the employee to inform the employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 98(6) — the last day for the employee to inform the employer` `the day the employer requires the employee to inform the employer` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the day the employer requires the employee to inform the employer` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 30)

§§ `Section 99 -- how the application is signed, and a change of name`

-- src:2689 | Application to be signed by applicant
-- src:2690 | 99 (1) An application for a Social Insurance Number shall be signed by the applicant in his own hand but where the applicant is unable to sign his own name, he may attest the application by making his mark in the presence of two witnesses whose names and signatures shall be shown thereon.
@ref Act s 99(1) (src:2689-2690)
GIVEN `the applicant signed the application in the applicant's own hand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is unable to sign the applicant's own name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant attested the application by making a mark` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of witnesses in whose presence the mark was made` IS A NUMBER
      `the witnesses' names and signatures are shown on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 99(1) — the application for a Social Insurance Number is signed as the section requires` `the applicant signed the application in the applicant's own hand` `the applicant is unable to sign the applicant's own name` `the applicant attested the application by making a mark` `the number of witnesses in whose presence the mark was made` `the witnesses' names and signatures are shown on the application` MEANS
        `the applicant signed the application in the applicant's own hand`
    OR  (    `the applicant is unable to sign the applicant's own name`
         AND `the applicant attested the application by making a mark`
         -- "in the presence of two witnesses": at least two (fork C6-F11)
         AND `the number of witnesses in whose presence the mark was made` AT LEAST 2
         AND `the witnesses' names and signatures are shown on the application`)

-- The result is one of three, because the text gives a time only when the duty has begun to run.
-- src:2691 | Change of name
-- src:2692 | (2) When the name of an individual to whom a Social Insurance Number has been assigned changes, by reason of marriage or otherwise, the individual shall inform the Minister of their new name, unless they have already so informed another authority empowered to receive that information,
-- src:2693 | (a) if the individual is employed in pensionable employment, within 60 days after the day on which the change of name becomes effective; or
-- src:2694 | (b) if the individual is not employed in pensionable employment but later becomes so employed, or is required to make a contribution under this Act in respect of their self-employed earnings, within 60 days after the day on which the individual becomes so employed or after the first day on or before which they are required under section 33 to pay any amount as or on account of the contributions required to be made by them in respect of those earnings, as the case may be.
@ref Act s 99(2) (src:2691-2694)
DECLARE `cp6 Time for informing the Minister of a change of name` IS ONE OF
    `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` HAS `last day for informing the Minister` IS A DATE
    `the individual need not inform the Minister of the new name`
    `no time for informing the Minister has yet begun to run`

@ref Act s 99(2) (src:2691-2694)
GIVEN `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has already informed another authority empowered to receive the new name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the change of name becomes effective` IS A DATE
      `the individual is employed in pensionable employment on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the individual later becomes employed in pensionable employment` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the first day on or before which section 33 requires the individual to pay on self-employed earnings` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `cp6 Time for informing the Minister of a change of name`
`s 99(2) — the time for informing the Minister of the new name` `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the individual` `the individual has already informed another authority empowered to receive the new name` `the day the change of name becomes effective` `the individual is employed in pensionable employment on that day` `the day the individual later becomes employed in pensionable employment` `the first day on or before which section 33 requires the individual to pay on self-employed earnings` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `a Social Insurance Number has been assigned to the individual`
                THEN `the individual need not inform the Minister of the new name`
           -- "unless they have already so informed another authority empowered to receive that information"
           IF `the individual has already informed another authority empowered to receive the new name`
                THEN `the individual need not inform the Minister of the new name`
           -- (a): within 60 days after the day the change of name becomes effective
           IF `the individual is employed in pensionable employment on that day`
                THEN `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS `the date a time limit ends` `the day the change of name becomes effective` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 60)
           -- (b): within 60 days after the day the individual becomes so employed or after the first day on or before which
           -- section 33 requires payment, "as the case may be"; when both have come, the earlier governs (fork C6-F8)
           OTHERWISE
                CONSIDER `the day the individual later becomes employed in pensionable employment`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN
                    CONSIDER `the first day on or before which section 33 requires the individual to pay on self-employed earnings`
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no time for informing the Minister has yet begun to run`
                    WHEN JUST payDay THEN `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS `the date a time limit ends` payDay (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 60)
                WHEN JUST workDay THEN
                    CONSIDER `the first day on or before which section 33 requires the individual to pay on self-employed earnings`
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS `the date a time limit ends` workDay (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 60)
                    WHEN JUST payDay THEN
                        IF workDay AT MOST payDay
                        THEN `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS `the date a time limit ends` workDay (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 60)
                        ELSE `the individual must inform the Minister by a last day` WITH `last day for informing the Minister` IS `the date a time limit ends` payDay (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 60)

§§ `Section 100 -- agreement with a province about assigning numbers`

-- src:2695 | Agreement respecting assignment of Social Insurance Numbers
-- src:2696 | 100 (1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Government of Canada, enter into an agreement with the government of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan under which the Minister may cause Social Insurance Numbers to be assigned to persons to whom Social Insurance Numbers have not earlier been assigned, on the basis of applications made by those persons to the appropriate authority in that province.
@ref Act s 100(1) (src:2695-2696)
GIVEN province IS A Province
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 100(1) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province about assigning Social Insurance Numbers` province MEANS
    -- the Minister may do so only with the government of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan
    province's `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`

-- src:2697 | Numbers deemed to have been assigned under Act
-- src:2698 | (2) Any Social Insurance Numbers caused to be assigned by the Minister under any agreement entered into under subsection (1) shall be deemed for all purposes of this Act to have been assigned under this Act.
@ref Act s 100(2) (src:2697-2698)
GIVEN `the Minister caused the number to be assigned under an agreement entered into under subsection 100(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 100(2) — a number caused to be assigned under an agreement is deemed to have been assigned under this Act` `the Minister caused the number to be assigned under an agreement entered into under subsection 100(1)` MEANS
    -- "deemed for all purposes of this Act to have been assigned under this Act"
    `the Minister caused the number to be assigned under an agreement entered into under subsection 100(1)`

-- Section 101 (lines 2699 to 2708) is a regulation-making power of the Governor in Council; see NOTES.md, coverage table.
